                <pb facs="0325" n="255" sameAs="frus:frus1934v04/pg255"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/3787: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gilbert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-06-04T14:00:00+01:00">June 4, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 4—12:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>132. Consulate’s No. 129, June 2,6 p.m., paragraph 2c, arms embargo proposal. In
                    addition to the states in its 1933 reply Italy has formally named Soviet Russia
                    and Japan. Question of communicating with those Governments is not yet
                    settled.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gilbert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
